T1  - Spleen-preserving distal pancreatectomy following neoadjuvant chemotherapy for papillary solid and cystic neoplasm of pancreas.
A1  - Das, Ganesh
A1  - Bhuyan, Chidananda
A1  - Das, Bhabesh Kumar
A1  - Sharma, Jagannath Deb
A1  - Saikia, Bhargab Jyoti
A1  - Purkystha, Joydeep
Y1  - 2004//
N2  - Papillary solid and cystic neoplasm (PSCN) is a rare neoplasm of the pancreas with low-grade malignant potential and favorable prognosis. We report an 18-year-old girl with PSCN presenting with advanced disease. The tumor regressed with six cycles of gemcitabine and cisplantin-based neoadjuvant chemotherapy; spleen-preserving distal pancreatectomy was then done. She is disease-free at 13 months' follow-up.
