A1  - Yasuda, T
A1  - Imaoka, S
A1  - Fujita, M
A1  - Kuroda, C
Y1  - 1997//
N2  - Intra-arterial infusion chemotherapy was given preoperatively to one patient with pancreatic head adenocarcinoma, in order to prevent local failure after surgery. Under an angiographic procedure, a catheter was placed in the gastroduodenal artery after embolizing the right gastric artery and gastroepiploic artery. Before surgery, 5-fluorouracil (250 mg/day) had been continuously infused for 2 weeks and bolus infusion of methotrexate (25 mg) with 5 micrograms of angiotensin-II had been performed every 3 days. As a results, the maximum diameter of the pancreatic tumor decreased from 3 cm to 2 cm on the CT-Scan. An extended pancreatoduodenectomy with portal vein reconstruction was performed. In histologic study, degenerative tumor cells were shown not only in the primary tumor but also in the extrapancreatic perineural invasion.
